  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer planar multilayer dielectric stack under frequency-domain plane-wave illumination. Stack topology: Air incident medium, then 24 alternating layers starting with HfO2, then SiO2 (Lemarchand), repeating (HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand), HfO2, SiO2 (Lemarchand)), terminated by Fused Silica substrate. Design variables: all 24 individual layer thicknesses in nanometers. Optimization uses gradient-based thickness tuning with perturbation initialization amplitude of 2 nm (reduced from 5 nm). Apply targeted local refinement pass on layer 3 (index 2, 0-based) and layer 6 (index 5, 0-based) due to their larger optical path length contribution. Wavelength bands: maximize transmittance in 1530-1565 nm, maximize reflectance in 400-700 nm. Incidence angle: normal incidence (0 degrees) as default since not specified. Polarization: unpolarized or both TE and TM averaged. Manufacturing constraint: total layer count is exactly 24 (within 30-layer limit). Materials: hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) only, resolved from material catalog. Performance targets are soft ranking preferences, not pass/fail gates.",
